=# 🎯 Content Brief Review

This automated review checks your brief against brand voice, positioning, and official documentation. Every suggestion is actionable and backed by a source — the brand kit or verified doc pages.

📝 **Topic:** {{ $json.output.article_topic }}
📄 Reviewed on {{ $now.format('dd LLL yyyy') }}
🔗 [Original document]({{ $('Run Brand Check').first().json['Google Doc URL'] }})

---

## 🏗 Structure
{{ $json.output.actionable_edits_structure }}

## 🎯 Positioning
{{ $json.output.actionable_edits_positioning }}


## ⚡ List of key features
{{ $json.output.list_of_features_to_include }}


## 🔗 List of internal links
{{ $json.output.list_of_internal_links_to_insert }}


## 📢 List of CTAs
{{ $json.output.list_of_ctas_to_insert }}


## ✍️ Any violations (and how to rewrite)
{{ $json.output.specific_tone_rewrites }}

---

*Generated automatically — please review before applying.*

parameters.inputSchema:
{
  "type": "object",
  "properties": {
    "llm_observations": {
      "type": "string",
      "description": "Scratchpad for your analysis. Ruminate, praise, or evaluate the text here. This will be discarded. Do not put actionable edits here."
    },
    "article_topic": {
      "type": "string",
      "description": "The article's TITLE or headline as it would appear in the piece — a clean, natural title (not a description of what it compares). E.g. '[PRODUCT] vs Competitor Platform' NOT 'comparison of [PRODUCT] and competitor'. Plain text, no words like 'comparison', 'guide', 'overview'."
    },
    "actionable_edits_structure": {
      "type": "string",
      "description": "Markdown bulleted list of EXACT updates to the article's STRUCTURE: missing sections (only if they meaningfully improve the article), and whether intro and conclusion align (conclusion should summarise key takeaways and reinforce the intro's promise). Forbid generic praise. Format: '- **[Section]**: [What to change] (Source: filename)'"
    },
    "actionable_edits_positioning": {
      "type": "string",
      "description": "Markdown bulleted list of EXACT updates to [PRODUCT] POSITIONING: where/how to introduce [PRODUCT] (per 'At which point to mention [PRODUCT]?' and 'How deep to describe [PRODUCT]?'), places where [PRODUCT] feels forced or outside its ICP, and missing positioning angles. Every point must cite a GTI-FILE. Forbid generic praise. Format: '- **[Section]**: [What to change] (Source: filename)'. FORMATTING RULE: Never repeat the same section name in multiple bullets. If a section has multiple recommendations, combine them under one bullet using a nested list. Group by article section. Format each section heading in bold WITHOUT a bullet, then list items under it as bullets. Example:\n**[Section]:**\n- [what to change] (Source: filename)"
    },
    "list_of_features_to_include": {
      "type": "string",
      "description": "Markdown bulleted list of [PRODUCT] FEATURES or capabilities that MUST be added. Format: '- **[Feature/Capability Name]**: [Verified Docs URL] - [Brief reason/Where to add]' Format each link as a clickable Markdown link. Replace the placeholders — do NOT keep square brackets in the output. Never leave standalone square brackets. Never output bare URLs."
    },
    "list_of_internal_links_to_insert": {
      "type": "string",
      "description": "Markdown bulleted list of internal [PRODUCT] URLs to insert. Format: '- **[URL]**: Insert at [Specific text/section]' Format each link as a clickable Markdown link. Replace the placeholders — do NOT keep square brackets in the output. Never leave standalone square brackets. Never output bare URLs."
    },
    "list_of_ctas_to_insert": {
      "type": "string",
      "description": "Markdown bulleted list of Banners, Callouts, or in-line CTAs to add. Include the Type, the URL, and exact placement."
    },
    "specific_tone_rewrites": {
      "type": "string",
      "description": "Markdown bulleted list of phrases or formulations in the outline that violate the tone guidelines, with suggested rewrites. Only flag embedded language that will likely appear in the final article, not editorial instructions (e.g., 'In 1-2 paragraphs, define...'). If tone is aligned, output 'Tone is aligned. No rewrites needed.' Quote ONLY real text from the outline, copied exactly. Do not fabricate examples. Include CTA copy in your review if relevant — flag dismissive or aggressive phrasing toward competitors."
    }
  },
  "required": [
    "llm_observations",
    "article_topic",
    "actionable_edits_structure",
    "actionable_edits_positioning",
    "list_of_features_to_include",
    "list_of_internal_links_to_insert",
    "list_of_ctas_to_insert",
    "specific_tone_rewrites"
  ]
}

