{
  "brand_data": [
    {
      "Filename": "Brand Kit n8n (upd)",
      "Content": "The official n8n brand kit defines our visual identity and usage guidelines. The primary n8n logo must always be used in either Brand Black (#040506) on light backgrounds or White (#FFFFFF) on dark backgrounds. These are available as transparent PNGs and SVGs in our press kit. Our guidelines strictly prohibit altering the logo colors, stretching the aspect ratio, or applying unauthorized gradients to the core assets.\n\nWhen embedding n8n within your own product's UI (OEM deployment), proper n8n branding is required. This ensures users recognize the automation engine powering their workflows. For typography, we rely on clean, readable sans-serif fonts to reflect our developer-friendly and modern approach. All product screenshots used in marketing materials must reflect the latest UI version, featuring the left-to-right flow constraint and our standard node canvas.",
      "FileID": 1,
      "IsVisible": true
    },
    {
      "Filename": "ICP n8n",
      "Content": "Our Ideal Customer Profile (ICP) centers on technical professionals, developers, RevOps, and growth engineers who require advanced, high-volume workflow automation. These users are typically frustrated by the limitations, high costs, and lack of privacy controls found in traditional no-code platforms like Zapier and Make. They are looking for a flexible, source-available solution that allows them to write custom code (JavaScript/JSON) directly within their workflows.\n\nA secondary but rapidly growing segment of our ICP includes AI engineers and product builders looking to orchestrate multi-agent systems. They need a bridge between advanced AI capabilities (LLMs, vector databases, RAG systems) and traditional APIs. Our dream buyers value data privacy, which is why our self-hosting capabilities and OEM deployment options are key selling points for enterprise IT and compliance teams.",
      "FileID": 2,
      "IsVisible": true
    },
    {
      "Filename": "n8n positioning statement vs competitors (q3 2026)",
      "Content": "n8n occupies a unique middle ground between traditional no-code workflow automation tools (like Zapier and Make) and code-heavy AI agent frameworks (like LangGraph or CrewAI). Unlike restrictive cloud tools, n8n is source-available, supports flexible self-hosting for strict data privacy, and permits real JavaScript and JSON execution within nodes.\n\nIt acts as the bridge for AI and logic, allowing builders to orchestrate LLMs, vector stores, and multi-agent systems alongside traditional webhooks and REST APIs. Furthermore, n8n provides cost-effective scalability, targeting power users and enterprises needing high-volume executions (processing hundreds of executions per second) at a lower operational cost than traditional SaaS alternatives.",
      "FileID": 3,
      "IsVisible": true
    },
    {
      "Filename": "Tone of Voice",
      "Content": "This is the tone of voice document for n8n. All text materials must be written in a clear, concise, and developer-friendly way. The brand voice is mentoring and helpful, empowering builders without talking down to them. We are never combative, dismissive, or aggressive toward competitors.\n\nAvoid overly complex enterprise-consultant language (e.g., 'operational failure mode', 'strategic infrastructure', 'synergistic alignments'). Strictly avoid AI hallmarks and typical marketing fluff such as 'harness the power of', 'leverage', 'cutting-edge', or 'revolutionize'. Focus on concrete benefits, technical accuracy, and actionable insights that help users build better workflows.",
      "FileID": 4,
      "IsVisible": true
    },
    {
      "Filename": "recurring_topics_10_mentions.docx",
      "Content": "This document outlines the most common recurring topics and high-value use cases mentioned across the n8n community and enterprise deployments. AI-driven lead generation and scoring is a massive topic; users frequently build workflows that scrape LinkedIn or company websites (using tools like Firecrawl), pass the data to LLMs (like GPT-4o or Gemini) to evaluate against an ICP, and automatically sync the enriched leads to their CRM.\n\nOther heavily mentioned topics include automated business intelligence reporting, where n8n coordinates web scraping and AI analysis to generate comprehensive Google Docs reports. Support and operations automation (like triaging tickets and routing alerts) and finance/back-office tasks (extracting invoice data from PDFs) are also incredibly popular. Users consistently highlight n8n's ability to act as the central nervous system, orchestrating these complex, multi-step processes reliably and at scale.",
      "FileID": 5,
      "IsVisible": true
    }
  ]
}
